      "value": "@{60ee9e81572cc51ad4e847e6|full_name} \n\nThank you for telling me. I certainly overlooked that.\n\nWhen I tried running it like this:\n\n         public override void OnPlayerJoined(VRCPlayerApi player)\n\n         {\n\n             if(player == null) { return; }\n\n             if (!player.IsValid()) { return; }\n\n             player.SetAvatarAudioForceSpatial(true);\n\n             player.SetAvatarAudioCustomCurve(false); // I tried true but same result\n\n             player.SetAvatarAudioGain(5.0f);\n\n             player.SetAvatarAudioFarRadius(5.0f);\n\n             player.SetAvatarAudioNearRadius(0.0f);\n\n         }\n\nIt didn't work as expected.\n\nThe sound doesn't attenuate, it's distorted like noise, and it's clearly broken.\n\nI guess this should be considered another bug, but it doesn't seem to solve my problem anyway.",
