  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "SetAvatarAudioFarRadius() is currently effective for AudioSources whose Spatial Blend is 3D, but not for AudioSources whose Spatial Blend is 2D.\n\nSetAvatarAudioGain() is effective regardless of 2D or 3D.\n\nNow, I want to stop uncontrolled loud avatars from harassing people in public instances, but I also don't think we should place unnecessary restrictions on the AudioSource of normal avatars. (e.g. heartbeat, small hand claps, etc.)\n\nI would like a way to maintain normal avatar volume while preventing harassment from a 2D AudioSource that can be heard throughout the world without limit.\n\nFor example, disable the AudioSource for avatars that are farther away than the distance set with SetAvatarAudioFarRadius(), or prepare separate volume settings for 2D and 3D, or whatever.",
